Package: prognostk
Title: Generic Prognostic Figures, Metrics and Risk Stratification
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Dan", "Williamson", email = "dannlbol@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A configuration-driven toolkit for survival / biomarker prognosis
    studies. Provides reusable functions for prognostic metrics (Cox modelling,
    bootstrapped survival prediction with confidence intervals, risk-group
    assignment, data-driven cutoff optimisation, external validation and
    calibration) and publication figures (oncoplots, distribution plots,
    Kaplan-Meier curves, forest plots and calibration curves). All dataset
    specifics (column names, survival horizon, thresholds, palettes) are driven
    by an editable YAML config so the same code applies to any cohort.
